Keep the progress animation timer while a bar animates

Style::timerEvent() marks an animation when it repaints a bar. The stripes
of a determinate bar move on every second step, so the loop repaints such
a bar on an even step alone. On an odd step a window whose only bar is
determinate reports no animation, and the timer of the animation dies. The
restart needs a paint, and no paint comes, because the dead timer asks for
none. The stripes therefore stand still, although the animated progress
option asks for the movement. A busy bar in the same window hides the
defect, because that bar reports an animation on every step.

The loop now separates the two questions. A bar that wants an animation
keeps the timer, and the repaint of a determinate bar stays on the even
step. The timer still dies on the step where no bar wants an animation.

The change sits on the branch work/style-paint of the local tree, as commit 4 of 21.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

